<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Old Pahang Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1470 CE – 1623 CE (approx.) · capital Pekan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Malay sultanate on the east coast of the peninsula, founded by a prince of Malacca in 1470 and joined to Johor in 1623.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pahang-sultanate">Pahang</a>, until then a dependency of Siam, in the mid-15th century. Around 1470 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansur-shah-of-malacca">Sultan Mansur Shah</a> of Malacca installed his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-shah-of-pahang">Muhammad Shah</a> as its first sultan, with his court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pekan">Pekan</a> near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pahang-river">Pahang River</a>. The dynasty was thus a branch of the Malacca royal house.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pahang-sultanate">Pahang</a> exported gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and forest goods, and its rulers kept close ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and, after 1511, with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/johor-sultanate">Johor Sultanate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-ghafur-muhiuddin-shah">Abdul Ghafur Muhiuddin Shah</a>, around 1600, issued a code of law and traded with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>. Pahang was often caught in the struggle between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> and the Portuguese.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1617 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iskandar-muda">Iskandar Muda</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aceh-sultanate">Aceh Sultanate</a> sacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pahang-sultanate">Pahang</a> and carried off its royal family. By 1623 the Pahang line ended and the state passed to the rulers of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/johor-sultanate">Johor</a>. A new Pahang sultanate emerged only in the 19th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1470 CE – 1623 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.96%;width:3.04%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1470 CE – 1623 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pekan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad Shah, Abdul Ghafur Muhiuddin Shah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/malaysia">Malaysia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pahang Sultanate (1470-1623)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1546&amp;focus=old-pahang-sultanate" aria-label="Old Pahang Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7550 2047 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Old Pahang Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7870 2303L7839 2352M7870 2303L7642 2226M7870 2303L7881 2378"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7839 2352h0M7642 2226h0M7881 2378h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7870 2303h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7870 2303h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pekan. <a href="/atlas?year=1546&amp;focus=old-pahang-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
